      "text_raw": "The voltage gain of the\ninput stage is A #125. The\nv\nbandwidth is limited by\nthe product R C and is\nF1 2\n178 MHz. The input resis-\ntance will thus be R /A\nF1 v\n#240 V. This is made low\nto reduce the effect of\nthe sensor capacitance C ,\ns\nand to increase the band-\nwidth to frequencies beyond\n178 MHz.\nThe input capacitance is\nincreased by the same\namount. It is now 4 pF.\nThe equivalent input\nnoise current is mainly caused by two components. The first one is the base current shot noise\nof the input bipolar transistor Q1. It is slightly smaller than the current noise of the feedback\nresistor R . Together it is about 1 pA /√Hz.\nF1 RMS",
